From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:20:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] fix(editor): "Hide completed" button of to-do lists covered the first item
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VERSION: 1.0 (2026-10-14)
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0014)

Problem: in a right-to-left to-do list the first item could not be unticked,
and the "Hide completed" / "Show N completed" button popped up over the text
whenever the pointer crossed the list.

Cause: the button was placed with a physical right: 0, top: -8px over the
first line. In RTL that is where the first item's checkbox and text start, so
the button covered the checkbox. It also caught clicks while invisible
(opacity 0) and appeared at once on hover.

Fix (CSS only):
- The button sits just above the list at the end of the first line (left in
  RTL, right in LTR, following the wrapper direction; a list with an explicit
  dir from ListDirection uses that list's end side), where the last line of
  the text before the list usually stops. It no longer covers any item.
- While invisible it is click-through (pointer-events: none).
- On hover it appears after 400 ms, so moving across a list does not flash
  it. When completed items are hidden it stays visible as before.
- Tables keep their own offset.

Files (1; N = new, M = modified, D = deleted):
  M shared/editor/components/Styles.ts

---
---

diff --git a/shared/editor/components/Styles.ts b/shared/editor/components/Styles.ts
index 60aa896..42c5278 100644
--- a/shared/editor/components/Styles.ts
+++ b/shared/editor/components/Styles.ts
@@ -1599,11 +1599,17 @@ li .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistWrapper} {
   margin: 0;
 }
 
+/* The "Hide completed" button sits just above the list at the end of its
+   first line, where the last line of the text before it usually stops, so it
+   never covers the items or the first checkbox, in either direction. It is
+   click-through while invisible (KMS patch 0015). */
 .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistCompletedToggle} {
   position: absolute;
-  top: -8px;
-  right: 0;
-  padding: 4px 8px;
+  top: calc(-1em - 14px);
+  inset-inline-start: auto;
+  inset-inline-end: 0;
+  white-space: nowrap;
+  padding: 2px 8px;
   font-size: 12px;
   background: ${props.theme.background};
   border: 1px solid ${props.theme.buttonNeutralBorder};
@@ -1613,7 +1619,8 @@ li .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistWrapper} {
   user-select: none;
   z-index: 1;
   opacity: 0;
-  transition: all 100ms ease-in-out;
+  pointer-events: none;
+  transition: opacity 150ms ease-in-out;
 
   &:${hover} {
     background: ${props.theme.buttonNeutralBackground};
@@ -1625,13 +1632,31 @@ li .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistWrapper} {
   }
 }
 
+/* Shown after a short pause, so moving the pointer over a list does not
+   flash it. */
 .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistWrapper}:${hover} .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistCompletedToggle},
 .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistWrapper}:focus-within .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistCompletedToggle} {
   opacity: 1;
+  pointer-events: auto;
+  transition-delay: 400ms;
 }
 
 .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistWrapper}.${EditorStyleHelper.checklistCompletedHidden} .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistCompletedToggle} {
   opacity: 1;
+  pointer-events: auto;
+  transition-delay: 0ms;
+}
+
+/* A list whose explicit direction (ListDirection) differs from the text
+   around it: the button goes to that list's own end side. */
+.${EditorStyleHelper.checklistWrapper}:has(> ul.checkbox_list[dir="rtl"]) .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistCompletedToggle} {
+  left: 0;
+  right: auto;
+}
+
+.${EditorStyleHelper.checklistWrapper}:has(> ul.checkbox_list[dir="ltr"]) .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistCompletedToggle} {
+  left: auto;
+  right: 0;
 }
 
 td .${EditorStyleHelper.checklistCompletedToggle},
